 minutes, the shortest that ended those tickets.
 
 ## Storage
 
-Sessions live in Postgres ([keep sessions in the database](../adrs/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)).
+The browser holds the session in a signed cookie. The cookie contains the member id and expiry; the signature
+lets a web server check it with the shared key. See [the cookie implementation](../../larder/sessions.py) for the
+format and verification rules, and [the storage decision](../adrs/0001-use-signed-session-cookies.md) for why it
+replaced Postgres.
+
+## Known limits
+
+- A member's session cannot be revoked individually from the server before it expires. Wait for
+  [the session lifetime](#lifetime) to elapse without renewal. If all existing cookies must be invalidated,
+  use [session key rotation](../runbooks/rotate-session-key.md), which logs everyone out.
 
