+# Rotate the session key
+
+For the volunteer operating deployments when the session signing key must change. Replaces the shared key and
+logs every member out; the team agreed to rotate only between pickups after the move to signed cookies.
+Owner: the ops volunteers.
+
+## Before you begin
+
+- Access to deployment secrets and permission to deploy all web servers.
+- A window between pickups, since existing cookies will stop working.
+- Read [the session storage decision](../adrs/0001-use-signed-session-cookies.md) and
+  [the revocation limit](../features/sessions.md#known-limits).
+
+## Steps
+
+1. Replace `LARDER_SESSION_KEY` in the deployment secrets with a new secret shared by all web servers.
+
+   Expected: every server's deployment configuration refers to the same new value.
+2. Redeploy all web servers so they load the new key. The [session module](../../larder/sessions.py) reads it at
+   process startup.
+
+   Expected: every running web server has loaded the new deployment secret.
+3. Check that an existing session requires login again, then log in and make requests through the web servers.
+
+   Expected: the old cookie no longer authenticates; the new session remains valid across servers.
+
+## If it fails
+
+If members are logged out when requests reach different servers, check that every running server loaded the same
+`LARDER_SESSION_KEY`, then redeploy any server still using another value. The code's `dev-only` fallback is for
+development; deployment secrets must supply the shared key. If the problem persists, involve the ops volunteers.
